<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47508" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἥρα</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἥρη</span></b> ,, ἡ, <u>Hera</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			16.432
		</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νὴ τὴν Ἥραν</span>, an oath
		of Athen. women, <i><span class="en">
			X.
			<u>Mem.</u>
			1.5.5
		</span></i>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> applied to the Empresses
			of Rome, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεύς</span> to the Emperors, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).333
			</span></i> (Thess.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3956b
			</span></i> (add.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name for <i>nine,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theol.Ar.
				58
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> the planet
			Venus, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				392a28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				96e
			</span></i>. (Perh. connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥρως</span> and Lat. <i>servo</i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡρϝαῷοι</span>,= <i>inhabitants of
		Heraea.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
